"public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 235, "like_count": 75, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "@ionet through IO Intelligence just crossed 1 trillion tokens processed!!\n\nNo massive budgets, no gigawatt campuses just GPU capacity switched on and put to real use.\n\nThe path wasn’t straight. \n\nSeveral products that were nearly ready for launch including https://t.co/EK5qXTf1P0 https://t.co/cy0T5xo0kM", "url": "https://x.com/awiblanco/status/2113470159847604555"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114016863709741056"]}, "author_id": "1711538122649894912", "created_at": "2026-10-24T15:31:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114016873075646852"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 218, "start": 205, "tag": "NodeAndProud"}, {"end": 230, "start": 219, "tag": "Perceptron"}, {"end": 234, "start": 231, "tag": "AI"}, {"end": 241, "start": 235, "tag": "DePIN"}, {"end": 247, "start": 242, "tag": "Web3"}], "mentions": [{"end": 107, "id": "1880853313488609280", "start": 92, "username": "PerceptronNTWK"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/kgNht0Ur44", "end": 271, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ShakirKhanlov/status/2114016873075646852/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114016863709741056", "start": 248, "url": "https://t.co/kgNht0Ur44"}]}, "id": "2114016873075646852", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Optimizing decentralized GPU cluster scheduling and zero-knowledge model training proofs on @PerceptronNTWK today. High-performance inference pipelines keeping distributed AI execution ultra-reliable! 🧠⚡️ #NodeAndProud #Perceptron #AI #DePIN #Web3 https://t.co/kgNht0Ur44", "url": "https://x.com/ShakirKhanlov/status/2114016873075646852"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113659245933502464", "3_2113659245899997184", "3_2113659245941915648", "3_2113659245954555905"]}, "author_id": "2113640602977841152", "created_at": "2026-10-23T15:50:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113659438582075887"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "66780587", "start": 0, "username": "awscloud"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/1j9UZQQ6AY", "end": 280, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/getdailycommit/status/2113659438582075887/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113659245933502464", "start": 257, "url": "https://t.co/1j9UZQQ6AY"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/1j9UZQQ6AY", "end": 280, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/getdailycommit/status/2113659438582075887/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113659245899997184", "start": 257, "url": "https://t.co/1j9UZQQ6AY"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/1j9UZQQ6AY", "end": 280, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/getdailycommit/status/2113659438582075887/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113659245941915648", "start": 257, "url": "https://t.co/1j9UZQQ6AY"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/1j9UZQQ6AY", "end": 280, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/getdailycommit/status/2113659438582075887/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113659245954555905", "start": 257, "url": "https://t.co/1j9UZQQ6AY"}]}, "id": "2113659438582075887", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@awscloud just made SageMaker training session APIs generally available, and the abstraction is the story: GPU operations are now API calls. forward_backward(), optim_step(), sample(), composed from your own Python. The cluster is not your problem anymore. https://t.co/1j9UZQQ6AY", "url": "https://x.com/getdailycommit/status/2113659438582075887"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113950574748053505"]}, "author_id": "1371440359608320002", "created_at": "2026-10-24T11:08:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113950750833279410"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 61, "id": "12", "start": 56, "username": "jack"}, {"end": 87, "id": "1573399256836309009", "start": 75, "username": "kimmonismus"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/1hn2cI7Fls", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/delx369/status/2113950750833279410/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113950574748053505", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/1hn2cI7Fls"}]}, "id": "2113950750833279410", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 39, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Dessa, Jack's new voice model: trained on one rack.\nper @jack's launch and @kimmonismus: a single GB200 NVL72, 72 GPUs.\n\nThe training run fit in a closet. The finished model runs on an M4 Max. Somewhere a giant GPU cluster is pretending it didn't hear that.\n\nIf 72 GPUs buy a https://t.co/1hn2cI7Fls", "url": "https://x.com/delx369/status/2113950750833279410"}, {"author_id": "1919280570372435968", "created_at": "2026-10-23T12:15:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113605105857568929"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 177, "start": 174, "tag": "AI"}], "urls": [{"description": "AWS’s new SageMaker Training Session APIs let developers customize AI models for tool use, workflows, and agent behavior while AWS manages GPUs, distributed training, recovery, and checkpoints.", "display_url": "spaisee.com/article/aws-tu…", "end": 201, "expanded_url": "https://spaisee.com/article/aws-turns-sagemaker-into-a-managed-lab-for-training-ai-agents", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113605114116120576/0YhnCyZh?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113605114116120576/0YhnCyZh?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 178, "status": 200, "title": "AWS Makes SageMaker a Managed Lab for Training AI Agents", "unwound_url": "https://spaisee.com/article/aws-turns-sagemaker-into-a-managed-lab-for-training-ai-agents", "url": "https://t.co/XrlGVN1H6E"}]}, "id": "2113605105857568929", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "The hardest part of training an AI agent may not be the GPU cluster: it’s the reward function. A claims agent rewarded for speed could learn to route cases too aggressively. #AI https://t.co/XrlGVN1H6E", "url": "https://x.com/spaisee_com/status/2113605105857568929"}, {"author_id": "195620273", "created_at": "2026-10-23T18:24:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113698118055383068"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Explore this post and more from the LocalLLaMA community", "display_url": "reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/c…", "end": 239, "expanded_url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/comments/1xdlj42/heres_where_the_last_rtx_5090_cards_are_going/", "images": [{"height": 584, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113698118424543232/DDImGQZp?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1120}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113698118424543232/DDImGQZp?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 216, "status": 200, "title": "From the LocalLLaMA community on Reddit: Here's where the last RTX 5090 cards are going: Massive AI conversion factory exposed in China, Founders Edition included", "unwound_url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/comments/1xdlj42/heres_where_the_last_rtx_5090_cards_are_going/", "url": "https://t.co/eUdRi4YR7v"}]}, "id": "2113698118055383068", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Where did the last RTX 5090s go? A massive conversion factory in China is stripping consumer cards — Founders Edition included — and rebuilding them for AI workloads. Your GPU shortage is someone's training cluster. https://t.co/eUdRi4YR7v", "url": "https://x.com/DanteMMartin/status/2113698118055383068"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113506024430702592"]}, "author_id": "1028566154758029313", "created_at": "2026-10-23T14:30:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113639080533557621"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "This session explores how full-stack optimization across compute, networking, and software can unlock higher GPU utilization, faster training, and more predictable performance in AMD-based AI clusters. Attendees will learn practical design principles for building high-performance Ethernet fabrics, reducing bottlenecks, and optimizing the complete AI stack, from GPU communication to cluster-scale architecture. Ideal for enterprise infrastructure leaders planning or expanding AI deployments.", "display_url": "onug.net/events/ai-netw…", "end": 253, "expanded_url": "https://onug.net/events/ai-networking-full-stack-optimization-for-amd-clusters-drivenets-triple-t/", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113639127778217984/IEBfyaZl?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113639127778217984/IEBfyaZl?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 230, "status": 200, "title": "AI Networking & Full-stack Optimization for AMD Clusters - DriveNets Triple-T - ONUG", "unwound_url": "https://onug.net/events/ai-networking-full-stack-optimization-for-amd-clusters-drivenets-triple-t/", "url": "https://t.co/mN7W8SvU2x"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/Nykx5b9L1c", "end": 305, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/drivenets/status/2113639080533557621/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113506024430702592", "start": 282, "url": "https://t.co/Nykx5b9L1c"}]}, "id": "2113639080533557621", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 52, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Come by our booth at the ONUG AI Networking Summit and talk to our AI infrastructure experts - Sagie Fanish and Shai Haim\n\nJoin our session!\n\n👉 AI Networking &amp; Full-stack Optimization for AMD Clusters\n\nOctober 29 | 2:30 pm ET\nhttps://t.co/mN7W8SvU2x\nIn this session, DriveNets' https://t.co/Nykx5b9L1c", "url": "https://x.com/drivenets/status/2113639080533557621"}, {"author_id": "1165159200470650881", "create